<Base
  title="Men’s groups"
  description="An online men’s group that works on your own time. Bondfires is an asynchronous video app for men’s groups: record when you can, your group answers when they can. Built by two men who needed it."
>
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">For men’s groups</p>
      <h1>The men’s group that doesn’t need everyone free on Thursday.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Most men’s groups die the same way. Not from conflict. From calendars. Bondfires is a private
        video space where your group keeps talking between meetings, with your actual faces, on
        whatever night you actually have.
      </p>
      <StoreBadges campaign="mens_groups_hero" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h2>What it looks like in practice</h2>
      <p>
        One guy records two minutes on a Tuesday night after the kids are down. Something real: a
        thing at work, a thing at home, a thing he hasn’t said out loud yet. By Wednesday lunch two
        others have answered, each from wherever they were. Nobody scheduled anything. Everybody
        showed up.
      </p>
      <p>
        That thread sits in the camp alongside the others. The Ember Rail at the top of the app shows
        who has answered and whose spark is still waiting. Over a month a group of eight men has said
        more to each other than they did in a year of monthly breakfasts.
      </p>

      <h2>Why video, and why not live</h2>
      <p>
        A live call needs eight men free at the same hour, and it rewards the fastest talker. A video
        thread gives each man the floor, for as long as he needs, at the hour he has. And unlike text,
        it carries the pause before the honest part. You can hear when a brother is not okay.
      </p>

      <h2>Private by design</h2>
      <p>
        Men’s groups run on trust. Bondfires camps for men’s groups are private and invite-only: no
        public profiles, no discoverability, no strangers. Videos are visible only to the men in the
        camp. We don’t sell data and there are no ads. What is said in the camp stays in the camp.
      </p>

      <h2>For the man who leads the group</h2>
      <p>
        You set up the camp, share one invite link, and spark the first Bondfire. Members join on the
        free app; only the leader needs Pro. Approve who gets in, set the rhythm, and let the Ember Rail
        do the nagging so you don’t have to. <a href="/for/groups">Here is how leaders set it up.</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Why we built this</h2>
      <p>
        Bondfires was built by two men whose own friendship kept dying in the group chat. We built it
        for our own groups first, and we run them on it. <a href="/about">More about us.</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Bring your group. Or start one.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Free to join, watch, and respond. iPhone and Android.</p>
      <StoreBadges campaign="mens_groups_footer" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

